# Line endings.
#
# The reproduce job in .github/workflows/model-check.yml compares committed
# model output against freshly generated output byte for byte. The outputs were
# committed from Windows with CRLF; CI regenerates them on Linux with LF, so
# every line differed and the job had never once passed. The check looked like
# it was enforcing the repository's central rule -- every published number
# traces to the model -- while enforcing nothing.
#
# Normalising here fixes the cause. The workflow also passes
# --strip-trailing-cr so the comparison stays about the NUMBERS rather than the
# line terminators, and so it gives the same answer run from Windows or Linux.
docs/sizing/*.txt   text eol=lf
simulations/recordings/separation-output.txt   text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF regardless of platform: CRLF makes the kernel look
# for an interpreter called "/usr/bin/env bash\r", which fails obscurely.
*.sh                text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.xlsx              binary
*.png               binary
*.pdf               binary
*.ico               binary
